   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `star INDEX` and made `list` put a `*` before starred notes. `python tools/check.py` passes: both unit tests are OK and the line-length check is clean. I ran it with `NOTES_HOME` set to a fresh temp directory, because the script requires that variable.\n\n- **`star`:** `fieldnotes/store.py` has a new `star(index)` that sets `starred: True` on the note at that position and saves the file. It raises `IndexError` if the index is out of range.\n- **CLI:** `star INDEX` prints `starred: <text>`. A non-numeric index exits with code 2. An out-of-range index prints an error and exits with code 1. `list` shows `*` before starred notes and nothing before the rest.\n- **Usage message:** it now lists all three commands.\n- **Test:** I added `test_star` in `tests/test_store.py`, covering a valid index and an out-of-range one.\n\nI didn't run the CLI by hand, so the `*` output in `list` isn't covered by a test. A negative index is also rejected as out of range, which seemed the safest behaviour.",
